issue(id="0009" status="open")
  title Expand the corpus and idempotence coverage for real Pug syntax
  user-story
    as-a maintainer of puggers
    i-want a broader regression corpus
    so-that refactors toward a richer syntax model can move quickly without breaking real files silently
  premise.
    The current generated docs corpus has been extremely useful, but it only
    covers a slice of the language and is skewed toward the HTML-converted
    examples we already materialized. As the formatter starts to parse more
    semantics, we will need a broader set of fixture sources that include real
    Pug syntax forms, intentionally tricky whitespace cases, and examples that
    should remain opaque. A stronger corpus will make all the other tasks safer.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Add curated fixture coverage for major Pug constructs that are not well represented in the current docs-derived corpus.
    criterion Include explicit idempotence tests, normalization tests, and failure-mode tests rather than relying on one corpus style alone.
    criterion Add fixtures for whitespace-sensitive text cases, code forms, comments, filters, includes, inheritance, and mixins.
    criterion Document how new corpus files should be organized so future task work can add targeted fixtures without confusion.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Decide whether converted HTML docs should remain one corpus tier while hand-authored Pug fixtures become another.
    item(status="open") Confirm whether we want snapshot-style assertions, inline expected strings, or both for different kinds of tests.
    item(status="open") Make sure corpus growth stays comprehensible rather than turning into a pile of unlabeled edge-case files.
